{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1736 (owner 2026-11-07, drafts approved 2026-11-08): ONE TRANSCRIPT ×4 for EVERY chat (a session, an agent, the Assistant, an app, a team agent): no 1:1 variant, no group variant, every chat reads like a group chat. ONE bubble ×4 = THE MessageBubble (web packages/ui `MessageBubble`, desktop crates/ui `message_bubble`, iOS ExpUI `MessageBubble`, Android `MessageBubble`; Exponential UI's `MessageBubble` macro carries the same `avatar` slot + press/href): the glass card bubble (16 px radius, its `HH:mm` bottom-right inside), `layout.maxWidth.phone` of the column on phones and `layout.maxWidth.wide` on web/desktop; on phones an `in` bubble (anyone but the viewer) takes `layout.maxWidth.phoneIn` of its column (the column right of the avatar), as wide as the trace cards beside it (owner 2026-11-13). A bubble from anyone but the viewer sits LEFT under its sender's AVATAR (THE Avatar at its default size `layout.avatar` px, `layout.avatarGap` px left of the column, top-aligned with the group's first row) and its NAME (the bubble's `author` line, 12 px medium muted, on the group's first BUBBLE only); the viewer's own bubbles sit RIGHT under the VIEWER's own AVATAR (#FEED-239, owner 2026-11-14, the mirror of the left: THE Avatar at `layout.avatar` px, `layout.avatarGap` px RIGHT of the column, top-aligned with the own group's first row; the viewer's image, else their initials in their hue) and no name; an own bubble has NO left inset: it may take `layout.maxWidth.own` of its column (the column left of the own avatar) on every width, the in bubbles keep theirs. SENDERS (`transcriptLayout(input)`, every mirror replays `cases` comparing the WHOLE expected array): an item is `message` (a card-less message row, a child's report, a pending input), `trace` (a tool, thought or subagent line of the agent's work, the raw session view's feed) or `full` (every card: a `Workflow` call's Work card (#EXP-1750), question, plan, to-do, suggestions, session card, picture, surface, event line, divider, locked pill; full width, never grouped). A `message` with `authorKind` `user`: `authorId == viewerId` = `own`; else the MEMBER (`kind member`, id = authorId, name = members[authorId].name, else `copy.formerMember`; the Avatar's initials in the member's hue). `authorKind` `system` = `full`. `authorKind` `agent` (or any message carrying `authorSessionId`): a CROSS-SESSION sender when `authorSessionId` names a KNOWN session other than `chat.sessionId` (a child's report, `sessions_send` from a session or an agent, the prompt a parent started this session with): `kind agent` when that session has an `agentId` (the agent's own avatar, id = agentId) else `kind session` (the muted session avatar with its glyph, id = the session), name = that session's `title`, `link` = its id. #EXP-1772 RELAYS (a cross-session bubble: another session's message, a child's report): its name sits ABOVE the bubble, outside it (the name line's size and colour, `copy.linkChevron` one space right of the name), on the group's first relay bubble; ONLY that name line is the press that opens the session on the back stack, the bubble itself is never a link; #FEED-238 (owner 2026-11-13) REVERSES the relay's no-fold: THE FOLD ×4 (`messageFolds`, `foldCases`) = every `message` bubble (own, member, the chat's agent, a relay, a child's report) whose text is longer than `fold.chars` characters or has more than `fold.lines` lines shows its first `fold.lines` lines and THE text button `copy.showMore` / `copy.showLess` under it (the existing one of the transcript's person turns); a long unbroken token (a base64 payload, a URL) wraps anywhere, never widening the bubble. The chat's own agent and a member keep the name inside the bubble. This REPLACES the `Started by` / `Report from` / `Message from` link rows and the `via MCP` card. Any other agent message = the chat's OWN agent: `chat.agentId` set = `kind agent` (id = agentId, name = agents[agentId].name, else `chat.title`), else `kind session` (id = `chat.sessionId`, name = `chat.title`; owner's answer: in a plain session the agent's bubbles wear the session title + the session avatar); `link` null. A `user` message carrying an `authorSessionId` of another known session (a session posting as its starter) is cross-session too. ORIGIN (one rule ×4, data first): `chat.originSessionId` = the session that STARTED the viewed one, from the synced rows (its `parentId`, else the agent conversation that started its root: session-chat.json `origin`), never from prompt text; `chat.fromStart` = the items begin at the conversation's very first message (no `Load earlier` above them). When both hold, the FIRST INPUT (a `message` item with `authorKind` `user`, or one carrying a known cross-session `authorSessionId`) reads as sent by the origin whoever the row names (in the raw session feed that first prompt is a typed turn), unless it carries that known cross-session `authorSessionId` itself (in a chat the prompt row names its sender, data wins); either way no later row takes the origin. The agent's own output is NEVER re-attributed: agent rows before the first input stay the chat's own. Parsing the prompt text (`inputCases`) is only the fallback for a session input the feed carries no author for. A `trace` item belongs to the chat's OWN agent sender (it never shows a name). An unknown `authorSessionId` falls back to the rule without it. GROUPING: consecutive non-full items with the same sender (kind + id + link; `own` = one sender) form one group; `avatar` = true on a group's FIRST item (#FEED-239: own groups too, the avatar on the right); `name` = true on a group's first `message` item when it is not own; `gap` (the space above the row) = 0 on the first item, `layout.gapInGroup` inside a group, else `layout.gapBetween`. The text of a session input on the device (`inputCases`, `crossSessionInput(text)`): the raw session view gets a parent's or child's message as a prompt line `Report from <name> (session <id>, ended): <summary>` or `Message from <name> (session <id>): <body>` (desktop `coding::pickup::input_text`); it parses to `{kind: report|message, name, sessionId, body}` (the pattern `^(Report|Message) from (.+?) \\(session ([^,)\\s]+)(, ended)?\\): ([\\s\\S]*)$`, the name the shortest prefix that matches) and draws as that session's cross-session bubble (`body` the bubble's text); anything else = null (a person's prompt). #EXP-1772 ONLY REAL MESSAGES ARE BUBBLES: a person's message and a real agent reply. A system input is THE inline MARKER ×4 (the feed's `Context compacted` row: a centred muted label between two hairlines, full width, never grouped): `feedInput(text)` (`feedInputCases`) reads a feed input as `{kind: marker, key, label}` when the device tagged it (`coding::pickup::input_text` leads a message carrying an `event` card with `[<key>] `: `schedule` = a schedule firing (`trigger_fired` without a name), `event` = an event firing or any other event, `pr_opened`, `pr_merged`, `pr_merge`, `pr_checks`, `session` = a session status line (`session_*`); the key must be one of `copy.markers`, label = `copy.markers[key]`), or, untagged (an older device), its body leads with the server's own firing text (`Schedule `…`` up to ` fired` = `schedule`; ``Event `<name>` (from `` = `event`); else `{kind: relay, …crossSessionInput}` for a cross-session input, else null (a person's prompt). A MARKER IS DRAWN ONLY ABOVE A REPLY (`markersShown(kinds)`, `markerCases`: kinds per feed row `marker` | `input` | `reply` (agent prose with text) | `other` (work, cards); a `marker` shows when a `reply` follows it before the next `input` or `marker`, every other row shows): a fire or event the agent answered silently draws nothing. A hidden marker is no transcript item at all (it never breaks a group). An agent turn whose text is blank draws nothing (no empty bubble).",
